nodecode-project-manager is a rewrite of AiSolve-me's AiSolve-me/hermes-project-manager:

https://github.com/AiSolve-me/hermes-project-manager
commit 2de4269baafc7399b7d4f92ad71b1d39205caf7b
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Tiboo / AiSolve.me (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the discovery of git repositories under the directories the
operator names, and the reads the plugin's five agent tools answer with --
list_projects, get_project, list_branches, get_recent_commits and
list_watch_paths -- together with the shapes they report (branch, last
commit, uncommitted files, distance from the upstream, branch tips from one
for-each-ref pass, a short-lived scan cache). They are Lisp functions and
five tools here, and /projects draws the list a person would look at.

Left out: everything the plugin does for its own dashboard -- the FastAPI
server on 127.0.0.1:9120, the bundled browser UI, the SQLite database of
scans and watch paths, docker stack detection, the worktree, diff, staging,
discard and push/pull actions, and the index.lock clean-up they need. They
are writes and a UI, and this cell reads the same repositories the way the
tools did, with watch paths in the config instead of a table. node/yarn/npm
are not needed: the one program it runs is git.
